{
  "id": "COMPOUND:14989 - PROTEIN:5826",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism of action linking the compound (1S,2R,7R,9S,10S)-6-acetyl-6'-methoxy-1'-methylspiro[4-oxa-12-azatricyclo[7.2.1.02,7]dodec-5-ene-10,3'-indole]-2'-one to the cancer cell line SMMC-7721. This compound is identified as a target of multiple pathways, including the sialyltransferase CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, which is itself a target of (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one and Mycalamide D. These intermediates are all implicated in the regulation of sialylation, a process critical for cell surface glycoconjugate formation and potentially influencing cell behavior and survival. The presence of multiple targets suggests a complex network of interactions, with the compound potentially modulating sialyltransferase activity to affect SMMC-7721 cell function. The evidence supports a mechanistic link, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
